  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Production of Polymer Modified Bitumen and Polymerised Bitumen Emulsions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because of problems between the project partners.Bolivia is a vast country with a national road network of more than 75,000 km. These roads can be found anywhere between an altitude of 300 m and 5,500 m above sea level. The pavement however, until recently, was not adapted to the specific requirements of the microclimate of those altitudes. Especially in high altitudes the impact of the climatic conditions on the road surface is extreme. With temperatures of the asphalt ranging from minus 15 at night time up to 40 degrees Celsius during the day, the bitumen becomes brittle and cracks in cold conditions and softens at higher temperatures, causing rutting and surface deformation.In order to reduce these problems, bitumen is worldwide modified by adding polymers, resulting in a more elastic and durable product with greater temperature stability. The PBM, recently being demanded by the National Road Agency and imported from Brazil, Colombia and Peru, is not adapted to the high altitudes in Bolivia.This project will import the base bitumen and set up an ISO 9000 certified production plant for PMB and PBE in the Department of La Paz. The PMB for high altitudes will be developed and tested in the ISO 17025 certified asphalt testing laboratory, according to the specifications of the client. The plant will be designed according to the latest European technology and environmental requirements and ISO 14000 certified.The initiative for this project was taken by the Bolivian company Latinoamericana De Proyectos SA (LAPSA), a services and consulting company involved in major public and private infrastructure works. The second Bolivian partner is Concordia S.A. Empresa Constructora, one of the leading road construction companies in Bolivia. Together with their partner from El Salvador, Empresa Terracera Nacional SA De CV, the companies will form a joint venture company, generating employment for 53 people. The project will also foster the introduction of new asphalt applications, including recycling of used pavements for secondary roads.</narrative>
  </description>
